            <div xml:id="d629">

                <pb facs="0757" n="745" xml:id="pg745"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">123 P 54/524: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-11-04T16:00:00+01:00">November 4, 1942—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 4—3:40 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6173. Personal for the Secretary from William Phillips. Your 5487, November 3, 7
                    p.m. I deeply appreciate the confidence which the President and you place in me
                    in asking me to undertake this important mission. Please assure the President
                    that I will do my utmost to carry out his purposes and that I am ready to
                    proceed to New Delhi whenever it is thought advisable. I look forward with
                    enthusiasm to the task. [Phillips.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
